<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chaguaramas</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Chaguaramas is a peninsula and bay at the north-western tip of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trinidad">Trinidad</a>, west of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/port-of-spain">Port of Spain</a>. Leased to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> in 1941 under the destroyers-for-bases agreement, it became a US naval base. It was chosen as the capital site of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-indies">West Indies</a> Federation in 1958, but the United States declined to give it up; after a campaign led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eric-williams">Eric Williams</a> the land was gradually returned and the base closed in 1967.</p></div>
